% The self-attacking argument as a classical debate (lk copy of
% self_attack.fspy).  P from a presumed refutation of P: the presumption
% is never captured by P's continuation, so this does not become the
% classical proof of P; grounded UNDEC, preferred P OUT, evaluation OPEN.
lk.

# Rationality fixture: self-attack (odd loop of length 1).
# One argument for P resting on the negation-as-failure default for P itself:
# pRule needs P->false on the term side, derived from a geled for P.
# Expected grounded labelling (graph labeller, see README.org):
#   node P: UNDEC on both sides; the argument's presumption site is UNDEC.

declare P:bool.
declare pRule : ((P->false)->P).

start argument SelfAttack P
cut ((P->false)->P) rule.
axiom pRule.
elim.
elim h.
cut (P) alpha.
axiom h.
by default.
next.
axiom.
end argument

graph SelfAttack
label SelfAttack preferred
evaluate SelfAttack credulous
